Q: Woocommerce Variation Price in Dropdown A: <p>And what is the question or advice you are looking for ? What i do in cases where i need custom UI is to just hide the default select and build my own. Good hook for it would be <code>woocommerce_before_add_to_cart_button</code>.</p>
<p>When we talk for single variation its easy. In case you need 2 , 3 or more attribute combos then its a bit more complicated.</p>
<p>In your case with <code>size</code> only option you need to loop your variations and populate your data you want to show/update. Here is example how should look like. For me is better to precalculate cm / inches and store in data attributes and toggle with js.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;div class=&quot;variation-row &lt;?php echo $row_class; ?&gt;&quot;
data-value=&quot;&lt;?php echo esc_attr($size); ?&gt;&quot;
data-variation=&quot;&lt;?php echo $variation_id; ?&gt;&quot;
data-stock=&quot;&lt;?php echo $in_stock ? '1' : '0'; ?&gt;&quot;
data-width-cm=&quot;&lt;?php echo $width; ?&gt;&quot;
data-height-cm=&quot;&lt;?php echo $height; ?&gt;&quot;
data-width-in=&quot;&lt;?php echo $width_in; ?&gt;&quot;
data-height-in=&quot;&lt;?php echo $height_in; ?&gt;&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;variation-size&quot;&gt;
&lt;?php echo esc_html($size); ?&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;variation-price&quot;&gt;
&lt;?php echo $price_html; ?&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;variation-radio&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Then in js you need to detect your select and trigger update on default woo variation form to set it properly. Thats all.</p>

Q: A question about computing upper Hessenberg form of square matrices in C : Avoiding costly matrix multiplication A: <p>You don’t need to explicitly form the full matrix (P) or compute <code>P * A * P</code>. In the Hessenberg reduction using <strong>Householder reflectors</strong>, the reflector has the form</p>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/iVfkuS1j.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer">enter image description here</a></p>
<p>so you can apply it <strong>implicitly using rank-1 updates</strong> instead of full matrix multiplication. (<a href="https://labs.acme.byu.edu/Volume1/QR_Decomposition/QR_Decomposition.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer" title="QR Decomposition — ACME Labs">labs.acme.byu.edu</a>)</p>
<p>Instead of building <code>P</code>, update the matrix directly:</p>
<pre><code>// Apply from the left
for (int j = i-1; j &lt; d; j++) {
    double dot = 0;
    for (int k = 0; k &lt; d-i; k++)
        dot += vec[k] * H[i+k][j];

    dot *= 2 * ins;

    for (int k = 0; k &lt; d-i; k++)
        H[i+k][j] -= vec[k] * dot;
}

// Apply from the right
for (int j = 0; j &lt; d; j++) {
    double dot = 0;
    for (int k = 0; k &lt; d-i; k++)
        dot += H[j][i+k] * vec[k];

    dot *= 2 * ins;

    for (int k = 0; k &lt; d-i; k++)
        H[j][i+k] -= dot * vec[k];
}
</code></pre>
<p>This avoids constructing <code>P</code> and reduces the work from <strong>two (O(n^3)) matrix multiplications</strong> to <strong>rank-1 vector updates</strong>, which is the standard way Hessenberg reduction is implemented in numerical linear algebra libraries.</p>
